    values:originalText "This Part imposes obligations on mortgage brokers and mortgage intermediaries. Mortgage brokers must act in the best interests of consumers when providing credit assistance in relation to credit contracts. Where there is a conflict of interest, mortgage brokers must give priority to consumers in providing credit assistance in relation to credit contracts. Mortgage brokers and mortgage intermediaries must not accept conflicted remuneration.  Mortgage brokers  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Financial Sector Reform (Hayne Royal Commission Response—Protecting Consumers (2019 Measures)) Act 2020 Compilation date: 15/09/2023 Registered: 21/09/2023  Employers, credit providers and mortgage intermediaries must not give conflicted remuneration to mortgage brokers or mortgage intermediaries. The circumstances in which these bans on conflicted remuneration apply are to be set out in the regulations. Subdivision B—Interpretation" ;
