doc:sch-3-sec-158lf a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "158LF Conflict between consumer’s interests and those of the credit" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "representative etc.  (1) If the credit representative knows, or reasonably ought to know, that there is a conflict between the interests of the consumer and the interests of:  (a) the licensee; or  (b) an associate of the licensee; or  (c) the credit representative; or  (d) an associate of the credit representative; or  Schedule 3  Mortgage brokers" ;
    cof:pageNumber "17"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2023c00239-sch-3-sec-158n a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "158N Conflicted remuneration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-158n ;
    values:originalText "Conflicted remuneration means:  (a) any benefit, whether monetary or non-monetary, that:  (i) is given to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, who provides credit assistance to consumers; and  (ii) because of the nature of the benefit or the circumstances in which it is given, could reasonably be expected to influence the credit assistance provided to consumers; or  (b) any benefit, whether monetary or non-monetary, that:  (i) is given to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, who acts as an intermediary; and  (ii) because of the nature of the benefit or the circumstances in which it is given, could reasonably be expected to influence whether the licensee or representative acts as an intermediary, or how the licensee or representative acts as an intermediary." ;
    skos:definition "Conflicted remuneration means:  (a) any benefit, whether monetary or non-monetary, that:  (i) is given to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, who provides credit assistance to consumers; and  (ii) because of the nature of the benefit or the circumstances in which it is given, could reasonably be expected to influence the credit assistance provided to consumers; or  (b) any benefit, whether monetary or non-monetary, that:  (i) is given to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, who acts as an intermediary; and  (ii) because of the nature of the benefit or the circumstances in which it is given, could reasonably be expected to influence whether the licensee or representative acts as an intermediary, or how the licensee or representative acts as an intermediary."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "6a20029795e75033aa891789f8f24f0564094c02fc56bf336f02d2a6e31b64c4" ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Definition of conflicted remuneration" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
