doc:sch-3-sec-158n a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "158N Conflicted remuneration" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Conflicted remuneration means:  (a) any benefit, whether monetary or non-monetary, that:  (i) is given to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, who provides credit assistance to consumers; and  (ii) because of the nature of the benefit or the circumstances in which it is given, could reasonably be expected to influence the credit assistance provided to consumers; or  (b) any benefit, whether monetary or non-monetary, that:  (i) is given to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, who acts as an intermediary; and  (ii) because of the nature of the benefit or the circumstances in which it is given, could reasonably be expected to influence whether the licensee or representative acts as an intermediary, or how the licensee or representative acts as an intermediary." ;
    cof:pageNumber "18"^^xsd:integer .

concept:c2023c00239-sch-3-sec-158na a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "158NA Regulations may further define conflicted remuneration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-3-sec-158na ;
    values:originalText "The regulations may prescribe:  Mortgage brokers  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Financial Sector Reform (Hayne Royal Commission Response—Protecting Consumers (2019 Measures)) Act 2020 Compilation date: 15/09/2023 Registered: 21/09/2023  (a) circumstances, in addition to those set out in section 158N, in which a benefit given to a licensee or a representative of a licensee is conflicted remuneration; and  (b) circumstances in which a benefit given to a licensee or a representative of a licensee is not conflicted remuneration. Subdivision B—Ban on accepting conflicted remuneration" ;
    skos:definition "The regulations may prescribe:  Mortgage brokers  Schedule 3 Main amendments  Part 1  Financial Sector Reform (Hayne Royal Commission Response—Protecting Consumers (2019 Measures)) Act 2020 Compilation date: 15/09/2023 Registered: 21/09/2023  (a) circumstances, in addition to those set out in section 158N, in which a benefit given to a licensee or a representative of a licensee is conflicted remuneration; and  (b) circumstances in which a benefit given to a licensee or a representative of a licensee is not conflicted remuneration. Subdivision B—Ban on accepting conflicted remuneration"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9f3a833e21a393076592406cb65352e515c0ec2aa01a70d2de6dada3ffbce2f7" ;
