concept:c2023c00239-sch-10-sec-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3 Application of ban on conflicted remuneration"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-10-sec-3 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subject to subitem (2), Division 4 of Part 3-5A of the National Credit Act, as inserted by item 5 of Schedule 3 to the amending Act, applies to a benefit given on or after 1 July 2020 to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, if the benefit is given under an arrangement entered into on or after 1 July 2020. (2) The regulations may prescribe circumstances in which that Division applies, or does not apply, to a benefit given to a licensee or a representative of a licensee.  Mortgage brokers  Schedule 3 Consequential amendments  Part 2  Financial Sector Reform (Hayne Royal Commission Response—Protecting Consumers (2019 Measures)) Act 2020 Compilation date: 15/09/2023 Registered: 21/09/2023" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subject to subitem (2), Division 4 of Part 3-5A of the National Credit Act, as inserted by item 5 of Schedule 3 to the amending Act, applies to a benefit given on or after 1 July 2020 to a licensee, or a representative of a licensee, if the benefit is given under an arrangement entered into on or after 1 July 2020. (2) The regulations may prescribe circumstances in which that Division applies, or does not apply, to a benefit given to a licensee or a representative of a licensee.  Mortgage brokers  Schedule 3 Consequential amendments  Part 2  Financial Sector Reform (Hayne Royal Commission Response—Protecting Consumers (2019 Measures)) Act 2020 Compilation date: 15/09/2023 Registered: 21/09/2023"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "33883758dc439711c26cd920bed773576970433e36af0492411ad8638be8af68" ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Ban on conflicted remuneration applies to benefits given after July 1, 2020." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <c2023c00239.pdf> ;
    dc:source "c2023c00239.pdf, p.22" ;
